# Local agent tooling — per-developer, machine-specific, never committed.
# Several entries under `.claude/` (`hooks`, `skills`, `workflows`,
# `output-styles`, `routines`) are directories in a working checkout, so a
# tracked file of the same name makes the checkout fail with "Directory not
# empty" for anyone who has one. Worktrees also live under `.claude/worktrees/`.
/.claude/
/.mcp.json

# The local stack config. Config discovery reads `./ovstorage.toml` FIRST —
# `ovstorage::default_config_paths`, and the REST and broker mains each default
# to the same path — so a committed one silently replaces every developer's own
# stack when their cwd is the repo root. The shipped templates live beside their
# crates (`ovstorage-cli.toml`, `ovstorage-mcp.toml`) under names discovery does
# not pick up, and say "copy to ./ovstorage.toml"; this entry is what keeps that
# convention from being undone by a `git add -A` during a local repro.
/ovstorage.toml
